            "RNASEH2B-LOF (AR 13q14.3 341aa): AGS2 — MILDEST AGS PHENOTYPE; may retain independent ambulation (unique to AGS2); p.A177T Northern European founder; ~35% of RNASEH2-subunit AGS; RNASEH2 complex removes genomic ribonucleotides (rNMP excision repair) → LOF → rNMP accumulation → cGAS/STING; calcifications + elevated ISG; baricitinib",
            "RNASEH2A-LOF (AR 19p13.2 299aa): AGS4 — SEVERE phenotype; catalytic A subunit; ALL THREE subunits required for trimeric activity — any subunit LOF destroys entire complex; A-subunit LOF = most severe RNase H2 loss; profound microcephaly + calcifications; DISTINGUISH from RNASEH2B (B=mild, A=severe, C=intermediate) by clinical severity not just sequencing",
